From 812a16b670a4d7b55ee51e696ff751b2b55d56df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:55:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] COMPK-MOTORB (web): every component of 29 pages checked
 (Motor Test, Shuttle Move, Vacuum Unit, Alert.Note, MyMessageBox, 9 setup
 pages, main.html and the Main.* panels, ShowMessage, testercomm, eventlog --
 4,270 components, each with a verdict) -- 457 fixed

* New ht9045_golden_kb.js: golden keypad flags / ranges where the generated wire data dropped ranges with min<=0 (Speed 54,
  YieldMonitoring 86, Temp_Set 188, OffSet 13, SetUp 9, Cleaning 9, Note edtLotID / edtLotCount); ShuttleMove 6 edits get
  their golden MOT[] soft-limit range.
* Setup.Speed: the 47 TUpDown spin buttons built from the dfm (Associate, Min / Max / Increment) -- they were missing.
* ht9045_wire_engine.js GB_NO_ASK + ArmSpeed_File, TestIF_File_YieldMonitoring, TrayForm, Temperature, Offset_File,
  TestIF_File_Cleaning, TestIF_File_VacuumUnit, ShuttleMove, TestIF_File_SetUp, AOAOffset (+ TfHotPlate bridgeSave): golden
  saves those without YES/NO; HW.MotorTest sbUpdate uses CFG.noAsk.
* Alert.Note: golden Reset / ShowErrorUnit visibility and Left for the 24 machine-picture panels (the flash was invisible because
  they stayed hidden; golden quirks kept: palOutSh1/2 never come back, palOCR stays); FlushLabel blink as golden.
* HW.MotorTest: English grid captions and pnlMotorAlias as golden.  Status.ShowMessage: the always-open window showed made-up
  values (Index Cycle Time 5.422, speeds 80% / 50%) -> "---".
* testercomm: cbbFullsiteTimeOut hidden as golden (it wrote general.ini); cbbRunMode + its button follow golden
  ShowSimulateItem (they could send ReContact / PlaceLoad / TrayFeed to the Handler at any time), caption "Send to Handler";
  spbAutoRetest / memoAlarmCode only with palSCKART; no live post while the Home demo is on.
Not changed, for EastSun (worklog section 4): Alert.Note keys skip golden's lock, Alert.Note START on PTI, the main toolbar level
lock, run-time keypad ranges C++ does not send, testercomm queued commands.

Verified: syntax OK (Temp_Set #10 = a "<script>" inside an HTML comment, as before); helper's headless Edge suites (Motor
Test buttons, ShuttleMove ranges, golden keypads on 7 pages, 47 spin buttons, Note visibility / blink, no-ask saves, testercomm,
16 pages load with 0 JS errors); ctest WebPageTable, WebMotorAccess, TeachButtonsGen 3/3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
